## What Middleware Does (and why it must exist)

```
// middleware.ts — this is NOT just an auth guard
// Its primary job is to REFRESH the session on every request
// Without it: access tokens expire and users get random 401 errors

CANONICAL TWO-FILE PATTERN (always use this — never inline createServerClient in middleware.ts):
  middleware.ts          ← thin wrapper at project root
  lib/supabase/middleware.ts ← updateSession() logic lives here

Cursor: if middleware.ts already exists, DO NOT create a second one.
        If lib/supabase/middleware.ts already exists, DO NOT recreate inline logic.
        One file, one responsibility.
```

```typescript
// middleware.ts — thin wrapper at PROJECT ROOT (never inside /app)
import { type NextRequest } from 'next/server'
import { updateSession } from '@/lib/supabase/middleware'

export async function middleware(request: NextRequest) {
  return await updateSession(request)
}

export const config = {
  matcher: ['/((?!_next/static|_next/image|favicon.ico|.*\\.(?:svg|png|jpg|ico|css|js)$).*)'],
}
```

```typescript
// lib/supabase/middleware.ts — all session refresh logic lives HERE
// (exact implementation in rocket-code-patterns-core.mdc)
// Do NOT duplicate this logic in middleware.ts itself
export async function updateSession(request: NextRequest): Promise<NextResponse> { ... }
```

```
If you need multiple middleware concerns (maintenance mode, rate limiting, A/B):
→ Use the CHAIN PATTERN from rocket-nextjs-patterns.mdc instead
→ That pattern REPLACES this simple two-file setup — do not use both
```
